Rosemary|rosemary]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Molasses|molasses]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Cider Vinegar|cider vinegar]]\n* Hickory chunks\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n#Combine dry seasoning and rub on pork ribs. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour.\n#Place hickory chunks in a 250 °F (120 °C) [[Cookbook:Smoker|smoker]] '''''or''''' a 250 °F (120 °C) charcoal [[Cookbook:Grill|grill]] set for indirect heat.\n#Combine remaining ingredients, bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] over high heat, and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] until reduced by ¾.\n#Place ribs in smoker/grill and cook 5–6 hours.\n#[[Cookbook:Brush|Brush]] ribs with tomato mixture and place on a high [[Cookbook:Grill|grill]], turning and brushing often until well browned.\n#Remove and let sit for 10 minutes; serve.\n\n[[Category:Barbecue recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using molasses]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Backyard Barbecue Ribs","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 slab pork spareribs","sourceText":"1 slab pork spareribs","amountText":"1 slab pork spareribs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp dark brown sugar","sourceText":"2 tbsp dark brown sugar","amountText":"2 tbsp dark brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 tbsp smoked paprika","sourceText":"3 tbsp smoked paprika","amountText":"3 tbsp smoked paprika","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tbsp salt","sourceText":"1 tbsp salt","amountText":"1 tbsp salt","